# Visitor copy — no meta, no UI tour

**Golden sentence:** The site *is* the lesson. Never narrate the layout, the cards, the playground, or how to use the page.

Visitor-facing = `content/pages/**`, lab `caption` / `teach`, compose fallbacks, nav labels, buttons. Not code comments.

## Forbidden (narrator class)

| Don't write | Why |
| --- | --- |
| "Each card below is one kind, with its own playground" | Explains the website |
| "The playground under a heading belongs to that heading" | Agent leftover |
| "This playground" / "this demo" / "Kind 1 of 4" | Labels the chrome |
| "Drag the scene. Hover the markers." | Tutorial for the UI |
| "Slide **Cover / diffusion**" / "Toggle messy vs calm" | Names controls |
| "The interactive demo loads with JavaScript" | Breaks the fourth wall |
| "Click here to learn" / "as you'll see below" | Tour-guide voice |

Teach **light** — skyglow, glare, a cover, red at night. The scene is already there. Don't announce it.

## Tone — teach, then give a path

**Golden sentence:** Direct, polite, clear. Education, then options. No sermons, no talking down, no soft riddles.

Brand tagline stays **Reclaim the night sky.** That is the line. Do not replace it with a softer slogan.

| Don't | Do |
| --- | --- |
| "The night sky can come home" (unclear metaphor) | "The night sky is disappearing — and so is our health." |
| "That's all this is." / "That's the whole invitation." | Stop when the fact is done |
| "The hope is simple" / "light that belongs" wrap-ups | A next step: letter, petition, product |
| "Why bad lighting is a terrible idea" | What good lighting does |
| "The Problem" / "Advocacy toolkit" | "Night light" / "For your street" |
| "cobra-head" / "full cut-off" | Street lamp with or without a shade |
| "biological cost" / "Full stop" / "the enemy" | Sleep, stars, a quieter bill |
| "fight" / "wrecking" | What to try instead |

Facts stay (AMA, birds, melatonin). After a fact, give an alternative or a path — home, street, or town.

```md
<!-- ❌ -->
Light at night isn't free. It has a measurable biological cost.

<!-- ✅ -->
Warm, aimed, modest light is a kindness — to your sleep, and to the sky we share.
```

```md
<!-- ❌ -->
Each card below is **one kind**, with **its own playground**.

<!-- ✅ -->
- **Skyglow** — the dome over town
```

```md
<!-- ❌ -->
Slide **Cover / diffusion** — the spear becomes a pool.

<!-- ✅ -->
A frosted cover turns the same lumens into a soft pool.
```

## Allowed

- Facts, stories, what to do on *their street*
- Jump links to a section (`[Skyglow](#skyglow)`)
- How to fix a *phone* or *fixture* (iOS Color Tint) — that's the subject, not our chrome
- Quiet `aria-label` on a lab (`Skyglow`) — not visible narrator copy

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No sentence that only makes sense if you built the page
- [ ] No control names, drag/hover/tap-the-i instructions
- [ ] Lab sit under a real heading — the heading is the label
- [ ] Swept every `content/pages/*.md` you touched, not just the one in chat
- [ ] Titles and nav are *for* something (sleep, sky, street) — not "the problem" / "terrible"
- [ ] No wrap-up sermons ("that's all this is", "the hope is simple")
- [ ] Tagline stays **Reclaim the night sky.**
